{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FSS7TNvSeTGjG5jyDrJPtG","type":"tool_result","content":"7338a3b Merge main: keep both the lint scanner and #40's triage roles\n2056013 ard(review:eng-review): #48 The change follows plan.md: scan, normalize.jq, Dockerfile, starter con…\n83b99fe feat: LLM scanner engine: run prompt.txt scanners as agent jobs… (#279)\n6a73aef ard(worker:engineer): #48 Adds a starter lint scanner role (golangci-lint per Go module plus `//n…\nb25c205 feat: Scanner: lint (#48)\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds a starter lint scanner role (golangci-lint per Go module plus `//nolint` directives, minus a human-owned baseline) so repos can file lint findings beyond a committed baseline. It fails closed on anything that would make findings vanish and autoclose.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/roles/scanners/lint/`: `scan` (POSIX sh, 0755, forced golangci-lint flags, `--baseline` mode, exit codes 0/1/2), `normalize.jq` (fingerprints, collapse, severity, fenced untrusted text, baseline parsing, three modes) and a pinned `Dockerfile`.\n- `internal/roles/testdata/lint/`: 15 synthetic cases, 3 real cases (`basic`, `nested_module`, `repo_config_new_only`) and `regen.sh`.\n- `internal/roles/lint_test.go`, `lint_scan_test.go`: golden, case-list, decode and untrusted-text tests, and a stubbed end-to-end scan test (argv, exit codes, read-only repo).\n- `lint_integration_test.go`, `lint_docker_integration_test.go` (tag `integration`); `scanRunArgs` doc comment generalised.\n- `config.yaml`: `scanners/lint` override and four `**/.golangci.*` protected paths. `roles.go` embeds `scanners/lint`.\n- `initcmd/body.go`: baseline bullet in the init PR body. Tests updated in `roles_test.go` and `initcmd_test.go`.\n- `Makefile`: `lint-scanner-fixtures`. Docs: `docs/proposal.md` (table, \"The lint scanner\", init and protected-path text) and `docs/layout.md`.\n\n## Testing\n- `go test ./...`: all pass. `go vet ./...` and `go vet -tags integration ./internal/roles/`: clean. Changed Go files are gofmt-clean.\n- `go test -tags integration -run TestIntegrationLintHost ./internal/roles/` passes with the host's golangci-lint 2.15.0.\n- The three real fixture cases were generated by running `regen.sh` with the host's golangci-lint 2.15.0, not hand-built.\n\n## Open issues\n- Not run here: the Docker integration test and `make lint-scanner-fixtures`. The Dockerfile pins were copied from the cve Dockerfile and are marked \"verification pending human\" in its header. A human must build the image and rerun the fixtures before merge.\n- `make lint` reports a gofmt error in `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`. That file is unchanged by this PR.\n- The plan named CLAUDE.md, but its Layout section now points to `docs/layout.md`, so that file was updated instead.\n- Not wired: enabling the scanner in this repo's own `.ard/` (with its baseline) and the follow-up issues stay with a maintainer.\ncomments.md\ndiff.patch\nissue.md\nprevious-review.md\n\nAdds a starter lint scanner role (golangci-lint per Go module plus `//nolint` directives, minus a human-owned baseline) so repos can file lint findings beyond a committed baseline. It fails closed on anything that would make findings vanish and autoclose.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/roles/scanners/lint/`: `scan` (POSIX sh, 0755, forced golangci-lint flags, `--baseline` mode, exit codes 0/1/2), `normalize.jq` (fingerprints, collapse, severity, fenced untrusted text, baseline parsing, three modes) and a pinned `Dockerfile`.\n- `internal/roles/testdata/lint/`: 15 synthetic cases, 3 real cases (`basic`, `nested_module`, `repo_config_new_only`) and `regen.sh`.\n- `internal/roles/lint_test.go`, `lint_scan_test.go`: golden, case-list, decode and untrusted-text tests, and a stubbed end-to-end scan test (argv, exit codes, read-only repo).\n- `lint_integration_test.go`, `lint_docker_integration_test.go` (tag `integration`); `scanRunArgs` doc comment generalised.\n- `config.yaml`: `scanners/lint` override and four `**/.golangci.*` protected paths. `roles.go` embeds `scanners/lint`.\n- `initcmd/body.go`: baseline bullet in the init PR body. Tests updated in `roles_test.go` and `initcmd_test.go`.\n- `Makefile`: `lint-scanner-fixtures`. Docs: `docs/proposal.md` (table, \"The lint scanner\", init and protected-path text) and `docs/layout.md`.\n\n## Testing\n- `go test ./...`: all pass. `go vet ./...` and `go vet -tags integration ./internal/roles/`: clean. Changed Go files are gofmt-clean.\n- `go test -tags integration -run TestIntegrationLintHost ./internal/roles/` passes with the host's golangci-lint 2.15.0.\n- The three real fixture cases were generated by running `regen.sh` with the host's golangci-lint 2.15.0, not hand-built.\n\n## Open issues\n- Not run here: the Docker integration test and `make lint-scanner-fixtures`. The Dockerfile pins were copied from the cve Dockerfile and are marked \"verification pending human\" in its header. A human must build the image and rerun the fixtures before merge.\n- `make lint` reports a gofmt error in `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`. That file is unchanged by this PR.\n- The plan named CLAUDE.md, but its Layout section now points to `docs/layout.md`, so that file was updated instead.\n- Not wired: enabling the scanner in this repo's own `.ard/` (with its baseline) and the follow-up issues stay with a maintainer.\n\nRequested next: `ard:review:eng-review`\nPR: [#283](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/pull/283)\nTests: passed\nLarge change: 1375 changed lines (warn at 1000)\nOutput: [.ard/48/worker-engineer.md](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/6a73aefd49867ea9735ace841343ca24d4a36e9a/.ard/48/worker-engineer.md) · log [.ard/48/logs/worker-engineer-20261123T212001.499Z.log](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/6a73aefd49867ea9735ace841343ca24d4a36e9a/.ard/48/logs/worker-engineer-20261123T212001.499Z.log) · job `01M854FBGX7VKDVYP9DX1ZXP1S` · attempt 1",